{"book":"Mark","chapter":5,"translation":"KJV","url":"/bible/mark/5","verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"And they came over unto the other side of the sea, into the country of the Gadarenes.","words":[["And",["G2532"]],["they came over",["G2064"]],["unto",["G1519"]],["the other side",["G4008"]],["of the sea,",["G2281"]],["into",["G1519"]],["the country",["G5561"]],["of the Gadarenes.",[]]]},{"verse":2,"text":"And when he was come out of the ship, immediately there met him out of the tombs a man with an unclean spirit,","words":[["And",["G2532"]],["when he",["G846"]],["was come",["G1831"]],["out of",["G1537"]],["the ship,",["G4143"]],["immediately",["G2112"]],["there met",["G528"]],["him",["G846"]],["out of",["G1537"]],["the tombs",["G3419"]],["a man",["G444"]],["with",["G1722"]],["an unclean",["G169"]],["spirit,",[]]]},{"verse":3,"text":"Who had his dwelling among the tombs; and no man could bind him, no, not with chains:","words":[["Who",["G3739"]],["had",["G2192"]],["his dwelling",["G2731"]],["among",["G1722"]],["the tombs;",["G3419"]],["and",["G2532"]],["no man",["G3762"]],["could",["G1410"]],["bind",["G1210"]],["him,",["G846"]],["no, not",["G3777"]],["with chains:",[]]]},{"verse":4,"text":"Because that he had been often bound with fetters and chains, and the chains had been plucked asunder by him, and the fetters broken in pieces: neither could any man tame him.","words":[["Because",["G1223"]],["that he",["G846"]],["had been often",["G4178"]],["bound",["G1210"]],["with fetters",["G3976"]],["and",["G2532"]],["chains,",["G254"]],["and",["G2532"]],["the chains",["G254"]],["had been plucked asunder",["G1288"]],["by",["G5259"]],["him,",["G846"]],["and",["G2532"]],["the fetters",["G3976"]],["broken in pieces:",["G4937"]],["neither",["G2532"]],["could",["G2480"]],["any man tame",["G1150"]],["him.",["G846"]]]},{"verse":5,"text":"And always, night and day, he was in the mountains, and in the tombs, crying, and cutting himself with stones.","words":[["And",["G2532"]],["always,",